    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d59">

                <pb facs="0429" n="215" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg215"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 46.</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Bailey to Mr.
                        Davis.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 44.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Consulate,
                                Hong-Kong,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1871-06-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 10, 1871</date>. (Received July 24.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Referring to my dispatch, No. 24, I have
                    the honor to transmit the inclosed decision of the chief justice of the supreme
                    court of this colony in the recent <hi rendition="#italic">habeas corpus</hi>
                    case of Kwok-a-sing.</p>
                <p>In as much as this decision relates to the Macao coolie trade, and also refers to
                    the Dolores Ugarte, I respectfully call the attention of the Secretary
                    thereto.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>DAVID H. BAILEY.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d59-a1.xml" xpointer="d59-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
